    "created_at": "2016-08-04T09:29:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-08-04T09:29:16Z",
    "body": "We do handle it as part of navigation in HTML. And I think you're correct that the flow in the standard should make sure that if the user agent wants to expose more detail there, that it's actually available. But in large part this is UX so user agents are already free to do what they want (as long as the document they create meets certain invariants which are probably not interoperable at the moment).\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
